# Code owners. GitHub requests review from the owner automatically when a PR
# touches a path they own, and branch protection can require their approval.
#
# The file must be named CODEOWNERS with no extension and live in .github/,
# docs/, or the repo root — anywhere else and GitHub ignores it silently.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins: a later line fully overrides an earlier one for the
# same path. Add narrower rules *below* the catch-all as reviewers are added.
#
# Note: GitHub never requests review from a PR's own author, so the catch-all
# does its real work on PRs opened by automation.

